=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported fault does not exist. The helpdesk ticket claims that the OSPF route for 172.16.30.0/24 (Campus 1 VLAN 30) is absent from the routing tables and that PC1 (10.5.0.1) cannot reach that subnet. Both claims are incorrect.

Direct inspection of the FRR routing tables on all three relevant routers shows 172.16.30.0/24 is fully present as an OSPF-learned route: router16 advertises it via its `vlan30@br0` interface (172.16.30.254/24), router7 receives it via its link to router16 (172.30.1.0/24 link), and router17 receives it via two equal-cost OSPF paths (through router8/172.29.10.x and router10/192.168.144.x). The route is installed in the FIB on all three devices.

Data-plane confirmation is equally clear: a live ping from PC1 (10.5.0.1) to PC12 (172.16.30.12) — an actual VLAN 30 host on switch3 — completes with 0% packet loss and ~2 ms RTT, identical in quality to pings to VLAN 10 hosts. The mswitch0 L3 switch has its `vlan30@br0` interface up and operational, and switch3 correctly bridges its VLAN 30 access ports through `br_vlan30` to mswitch0.

The network is fully healthy. No corrective action is required. The ticket should be closed as a false alarm; the submitter likely observed a transient condition (such as post-boot OSPF convergence delay) and filed before the network had settled.
=== END ===